1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,650
[This series contains scenes of violence,
self-harm, and potential triggers.]

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:05,220
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

3
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:46,030
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

4
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:51,980
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

5
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:54,740
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

6
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:57,680
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

7
00:01:14,130 --> 00:01:15,840
[Yoo Dohyun]

8
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:17,350
[Cho Chanhyeon]

9
00:01:17,470 --> 00:01:19,010
[Ko Gyeol]

10
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:23,980
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

11
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:31,130
But the problem is,

12
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:34,710
because of that,
he always crosses the line

13
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:37,240
and creates trouble.

14
00:01:40,979 --> 00:01:43,570
[Where are you?]

15
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:43,420
Where are you?

16
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,060
What does it matter to me
where he is and what he's doing?

17
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:02,020
Hey, you...

18
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:04,600
Open the door for me.

19
00:02:10,539 --> 00:02:12,050
You...

20
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:16,950
Why are you here when
you're this hurt? Go to the hospital.

21
00:02:16,950 --> 00:02:18,030
I came to see you.

22
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,340
What?

23
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:21,650
To see if you're okay.

24
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:24,200
I have to see it with my own eyes
to be at ease.

25
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,790
Can you still walk?

26
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:36,829
This feels more stable.

27
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,310
I guess you're not that hurt.

28
00:02:46,530 --> 00:02:49,460
Keep your voice down.
If Mr. Pan wakes up, we're dead.

29
00:02:50,970 --> 00:02:52,460
Die, Lee Won, die!

30
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:53,880
Go to hell!

31
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:56,600
I'm so scared.

32
00:02:57,290 --> 00:02:58,730
I don't want to die.

33
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,460
Smile.

34
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:09,830
Did you

35
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,780
end up like this because of me?

36
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,340
I'm right, aren't I?

37
00:03:19,550 --> 00:03:21,100
Why...

38
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,800
Why are you going to such lengths for me?

39
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:31,550
What about you?

40
00:03:32,829 --> 00:03:33,810
Huh?

41
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:38,460
Why do you absolutely
need to get that song back?

42
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,190
I want to at least protect his dream.

43
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:46,860
You do that—protect his dream.

44
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:51,800
I'll protect you and your dream.

45
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:54,060
What are you talking about?

46
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,420
You've bled so much.

47
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:05,360
What are all these?

48
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,420
Just some

49
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,210
old scars?

50
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:10,960
Right, so how did you get them?

51
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,190
They're all healed. It's nothing.

52
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:14,300
I'm used to it.

53
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,779
No one gets used to getting hurt.

54
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:34,540
Smile.

55
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,490
What?

56
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,970
Like how you smiled on stage just now.

57
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:41,180
Let me see that smile.

58
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:45,000
You do look ridiculous right now.

59
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:47,320
But I don't smile on demand.

60
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:49,150
Tsk.

61
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:53,030
You heard me sing.

62
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,120
How was it?

63
00:04:56,110 --> 00:04:57,200
Well,

64
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,630
I'm not sure.

65
00:05:00,350 --> 00:05:02,800
I wasn't paying attention to your singing.

66
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:05,220
I was too distracted by your pretty face.

67
00:05:06,490 --> 00:05:07,760
Don't be stupid.

68
00:05:11,130 --> 00:05:12,730
Did you get a concussion too?

69
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,290
Ah!

70
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:16,400
No wonder.

71
00:05:16,590 --> 00:05:18,780
You look so pretty now too.

72
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:23,470
Be quiet. Mr. Pan is asleep.

73
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:28,900
I told you to be quiet.

74
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:37,690
What are you doing?

75
00:05:42,830 --> 00:05:45,950
This is the most effective way
to shut me up.

76
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:58,050
Are you out of your mind?

77
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,780
Yeah.

78
00:06:01,490 --> 00:06:03,090
Don't answer.

79
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:28,010
This is actually better.

80
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:29,230
So thrilling.

81
00:06:29,610 --> 00:06:31,160
You're really crazy—

82
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:32,920
Stay quiet,

83
00:06:33,170 --> 00:06:34,380
or we'll get caught.

84
00:06:46,470 --> 00:06:47,550
Hanyul.

85
00:06:48,210 --> 00:06:49,280
Hanyul.

86
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,960
You're doing good, Hanyul.

87
00:06:52,090 --> 00:06:53,570
Here, good job.

88
00:07:53,290 --> 00:07:54,610
Ugh, damn it.

89
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:00,120
I'm up.

90
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,480
Hey, Hanyul! It's time for training.

91
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,470
Get it together.

92
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:11,930
Hey, did you sleep...

93
00:08:16,570 --> 00:08:18,180
What the hell are you doing

94
00:08:18,370 --> 00:08:19,730
in my sacred studio?

95
00:08:19,950 --> 00:08:21,120
Get up now!

96
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:30,930
You're supposed to be writing songs,

97
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:34,500
and you, working on your singing.
I swear I'm gonna...

98
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:36,150
I'm to blame.

99
00:08:36,270 --> 00:08:39,280
If you're going to scold anyone, scold me.

100
00:08:39,590 --> 00:08:41,190
He didn't do anything wrong.

101
00:08:42,409 --> 00:08:45,300
You've got to be kidding me.

102
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:50,500
I was just a little cold,
so I hugged him. That's all.

103
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,140
Cold? In this summer heat?

104
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:56,500
Then I was a little hot, so I...

105
00:08:56,950 --> 00:08:58,070
Get out.

106
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,510
Get out of here!

107
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:00,830
For crying out loud!

108
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:04,830
Pan.

109
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,140
I'm too sexy right now.

110
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,580
What? You want me to wear this?

111
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:19,510
Wear it and get out!

112
00:09:19,650 --> 00:09:21,270
Get lost! Shoo!

113
00:09:24,710 --> 00:09:26,020
Is this right?

114
00:09:29,850 --> 00:09:31,230
Mr. Pan!

115
00:09:31,350 --> 00:09:33,580
What brings you all the way out here?

116
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:38,070
What are you doing?

117
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:39,450
Here.

118
00:09:39,550 --> 00:09:40,860
Oh, my shirt?

119
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:51,810
Here.

120
00:09:52,370 --> 00:09:53,380
What?

121
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,740
Wash it again for me.

122
00:09:55,070 --> 00:09:56,240
Why should I?

123
00:09:57,110 --> 00:09:58,950
Why can't I take this off?

124
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:01,590
Don't move.

125
00:10:01,610 --> 00:10:03,580
Your hair is caught on the button.

126
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:15,020
I'll let you off today.

127
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:31,920
["Sound of Dawn" by Adolph]

128
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:35,810
This is Adolph's sheet music.

129
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:37,600
Why is it with you?

130
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:39,090
I'll give it all to you.

131
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:40,870
Come with me.

132
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,720
Just you and me.

133
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:09,350
It's really been a long time
since we visited our school, hasn't it?

134
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:11,220
I've always wanted to come back.

135
00:11:14,650 --> 00:11:16,220
What about the sheet music?

136
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,290
Don't you want it?

137
00:11:21,930 --> 00:11:23,390
You're still the same,

138
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:26,000
always putting Adolph before me.

139
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:30,050
Cut the crap.

140
00:11:30,510 --> 00:11:32,490
Where's the rest of his sheet music?

141
00:11:32,490 --> 00:11:35,260
Probably at... my house.

142
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,250
Unbelievable.

143
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:42,190
I'll give you one page every time we meet.

144
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:45,580
Sound of Dawn...

145
00:11:49,210 --> 00:11:51,830
Why did you release Adolph's song
as your own?

146
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:55,780
I thought it might bring you to me.

147
00:11:57,130 --> 00:11:58,590
You're telling me

148
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:00,360
you stole Adolph's song

149
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,830
just to bait me?

150
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:04,680
To me, it wasn't bait.

151
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:06,330
What?

152
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:08,400
It was a path,

153
00:12:09,430 --> 00:12:11,630
a path for you to come back to me.

154
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:16,140
This is making me sick.

155
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,700
Those memories with you

156
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:20,960
all make me sick.

157
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:23,380
But do you know what's really sickening?

158
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:27,240
Whenever I miss Adolph and
reminisce about him, you're always there.

159
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:30,980
That's why I can't even
think about Adolph.

160
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:33,410
Why did you kill him?

161
00:12:33,990 --> 00:12:36,050
Why did you kill Adolph?

162
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,320
You're saying...

163
00:12:38,670 --> 00:12:40,240
I killed him?

164
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,850
You did.

165
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,470
No, Hanyul.

166
00:12:44,790 --> 00:12:46,250
Then what is it?

167
00:12:46,650 --> 00:12:48,140
Tell me!

168
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:54,720
Yo, it's Herod!

169
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:56,400
I've never seen a celebrity before!

170
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,920
-I want a selfie!
-Take pictures!

171
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,050
-Come here.
-Me too.

172
00:12:59,070 --> 00:13:00,590
Why are you at our school?

173
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,090
Herod, let us see your face!

174
00:13:02,050 --> 00:13:03,580
[Saebyeok Entertainment:
I like your voice. Reach out anytime!]

175
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,590
Herod, let us see your face.

176
00:13:03,590 --> 00:13:04,700
Wow, so handsome.

177
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:06,680
He's so handsome.

178
00:13:06,690 --> 00:13:07,820
Where are you going?

179
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:11,070
Stop at nothing to get what you want.

180
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:19,820
You refused to take over the company
and insisted on being an idol,

181
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:18,260
[Y-route takes second place
on this week's music show]

182
00:13:19,850 --> 00:13:22,010
but you can't even get first place?

183
00:13:23,470 --> 00:13:25,690
Pathetic.

184
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:33,350
Is it taken care of?

185
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,900
Make sure there are no loose ends.

186
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,990
We don't need any rumors spreading.

187
00:13:50,650 --> 00:13:52,250
First place

188
00:13:52,350 --> 00:13:53,980
is yours now.

189
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:14,650
It may fade into the distance,
yet it still reaches toward you.

190
00:14:14,830 --> 00:14:16,910
The sound of dawn,

191
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,520
amid the stars that have
quietly fallen into slumber.

192
00:14:20,770 --> 00:14:24,490
Even as it softly echoes...

193
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:33,690
Dawn always comes softly,

194
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:37,730
leaving secret tears behind.

195
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:40,980
Hey.

196
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:43,150
Let's take a picture.

197
00:14:43,830 --> 00:14:44,860
Look here.

198
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,280
One, two, three!

199
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:51,900
Look at the camera!

200
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:54,560
Herod! One, two, three.

201
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:36,710
[Saebyeok Entertainment:
I like your voice. Reach out anytime!]

202
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:38,260
[Head of Artist Development: Go Hyunwoo]

203
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:54,920
Hello.

204
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,650
I'm calling you on behalf of Lee Hanyul.

205
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:01,560
I heard you left him a business card.

206
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,400
Are you still interested
in working with him?
